.TH NIGHTHAWK 1 "October 2026" "NIGHTHAWK 2.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
nighthawk \- graphical Nmap front end
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nighthawk
.RI [ --help | -h ]
.RI [ --version | -V ]
.br
.B ./scanner.py
.RI [ --help | -h ]
.RI [ --version | -V ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
NIGHTHAWK is a Tkinter graphical interface for Nmap. It builds validated Nmap commands, streams scan output, and creates HTML, JSON, CSV, and text reports.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR -h , " --help"
Print usage, requirements, and report location, then exit.
.TP
.BR -V , " --version"
Print the NIGHTHAWK version, then exit.
.SH REQUIREMENTS
Python 3.9 or newer with Tkinter and Nmap on PATH are required. Run
.B ./requirements.txt
to check prerequisites. On Kali or another apt-based system, run
.B sudo ./requirements.txt
to install missing packages.
.SH USAGE
Run ordinary scans as a regular user:
.PP
.B ./scanner.py
.PP
For authorized scan modes requiring raw-packet privileges, preserve the display environment:
.PP
.B sudo -E ./scanner.py
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ./reports/nighthawk_YYYYMMDD_HHMMSS_<id>.{html,json,csv,txt}
Generated reports.
.TP
.I ./scanner.py
The graphical application.
.TP
.I ./requirements.txt
Prerequisite checker and installer.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B nighthawk --help
Show command-line help.
.TP
.B ./requirements.txt
Check Python, Tkinter, and Nmap.
.TP
.B sudo -E ./scanner.py
Start the GUI for authorized privileged scans.
.SH PRIVILEGES
TCP Connect and most ping discovery scans work as a regular user. TCP SYN, UDP, FIN, Xmas, NULL, ACK, Window, Maimon, OS detection, fragmentation, decoys, bad-checksum, and idle scans commonly require root or raw-packet privileges.
.SH TROUBLESHOOTING
If Nmap is not found, install it and confirm
.B nmap --version .
If Tkinter cannot be imported, install the distribution's Tkinter package, such as
.B python3-tk
on Kali. If the GUI cannot open through sudo, use
.B sudo -E
from a graphical terminal.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR nmap (1)
.SH DISCLAIMER
Only scan hosts you own or have permission to test.
.SH AUTHOR
Ratnadeep Bose.
